From 1d6ef9f7faf28ce61f566f07ea5fb40c3aac2be6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: batya <batya@github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:56:27 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 06/16] fix(ui): a closed session stays closed, and our own
 lines use a plain hyphen

Sessions live in the window until the service owns them (stage 2), and that
state is now remembered the way the message log is: closing a session and
reloading came back with it open, which is simply wrong. The starting sessions
also get real dates instead of 1970.

Our own lines - code comments, interface strings and notes - now use a plain
hyphen. Author lines we never touched are left exactly as they are, and the two
author comments we had rewritten keep their original wording.
